keywords:
  - ultra-wideband
  - DW1000
  - indoor localization
  - real-time location system
  - moving horizon estimation
  - mobile robots
abstract: >-
  DUNE is an open-source indoor positioning system for mobile robots built on
  commodity DW1000 transceivers, spanning the complete pipeline from firmware,
  ranging protocol and channel scheduling to calibration, anchor survey,
  localization, filtering and validation. At its core is a rigid-body
  moving-horizon estimator that recovers a single vehicle pose from dual-tag
  ranging, making the inter-tag baseline exact by construction rather than a
  tunable penalty while simultaneously recovering heading.
